# GitHub — no Cursor metadata

Anything written to GitHub (issues, comments, PRs, PR bodies, labels, API payloads, commits pushed to the remote) must carry **no Cursor author, co-author, trailer, badge, or metadata**.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made with Cursor`, Cursor footers, branding, model names, or “generated by” lines to titles or bodies.
- Do not invent a Cursor Git identity; use the authenticated `gh` / git user only.
- Do not add Cursor-related labels, projects, or custom fields.
